What was taken from SearXNG
---------------------------
Only behaviour, interfaces, configuration shapes and data were ported; no
Python code was copied line by line. The following are derived from upstream:

  * the query syntax (\`!engine\`, \`!category\`, \`:language\`, \`<timeout\`, \`!!bang\`),
  * the result merging and scoring rules (\`searx/results.py\`),
  * the engine settings format and the engine defaults (\`searx/settings.yml\`),
  * the search API parameters and the response fields (\`searx/webapp.py\`),
  * the engine request URLs, parameters and result fields
    (\`searx/engines/*.py\`), re-implemented in Rust,
  * the locale table (\`searx/sxng_locales.py\`, generated file),
  * the plugin behaviours (\`searx/plugins/*.py\`).

Because of that derivation this crate is distributed under the same licence,
AGPL-3.0-or-later. If you publish a modified version — including running a
modified instance as a network service — section 13 of the AGPL requires you
to offer the corresponding source to its users.

Third party data
----------------
The bundled external bang list is a reduced, hand written table; upstream ships
a much larger compressed trie (\`searx/data/external_bangs.json\`) under the
same licence.

