Using RustXNG from an MIT/Apache project
----------------------------------------
  RustXNG is AGPL-3.0-or-later, so code that links it inherits AGPL.
  Running it as a separate program (spawning the binary, or talking to its
  HTTP API on 127.0.0.1) keeps the caller under its own licence; this is how
  rustdsh (MIT) integrates it.

  AGPL section 13: if you run a modified RustXNG as a network service, users
  interacting with it must be offered the corresponding source.
